    {
      "id": "s05",
      "index": 4,
      "text": "Before installing the air cleaner on the engine, check the air inlet housing for dirt. If the service period has been too long, or if dust-laden air has been leaking past the air cleaner to the air inlet housing seals, the inlet will be dirty. This will serve as a good check on the servicing of the air cleaner. When installing the cleaner (and its seal) on the inlet housing, be sure the cleaner seats properly, then tighten the wingbolt securely until the cleaner is rigidly mounted.",
